# Force LF line endings for scripts that must run on Linux (Pawsey Setonix).
# A Windows CRLF ending in a `#!/bin/bash` shebang (or any shell/slurm line)
# breaks with "bad interpreter" / slurm parse errors. This rule makes the
# committed blob always LF regardless of each machine's `core.autocrlf`.
*.sbatch  text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf

# Python is tolerant of either, but LF keeps diffs clean across Win/Linux.
*.py      text eol=lf
